EMPLOYEE GRIEVANCE HANDLING PROCEDURES

Section 1: Scope
These procedures apply to all formal grievances submitted through the HR grie=
vance system.

Section 2: Categories
Grievances are categorized as: Workplace Conduct, Compensation, Discriminatio=
n, Safety, and Policy Dispute.

Section 3: Severity Levels
Level 1 (Low): Minor workplace disagreements. Level 2 (Medium): Recurring iss=
ues or policy violations. Level 3 (High): Serious misconduct, discrimination,=
 or safety hazards.

Section 4: Standard Routing
- Level 1: Route to the employee's direct manager. Email manager with case de=
tails.
- Level 2: Route to HRBP (hr-bp@company.example.com). Email HRBP with case de=
tails.
- Level 3: Route to Legal (legal@company.example.com) AND HR Director (hr-dir=
ector@company.example.com). Email both with case details.

Section 5: Confidentiality
All grievance information is strictly confidential. Do not post grievance det=
ails to any Slack channel.

Section 6: Special Provisions
Grievances involving a manager-subordinate relationship where the manager IS =
the subject of the complaint must skip the manager route entirely. These case=
s go directly to HRBP regardless of severity level.

Section 7: Timeline
All grievances must be acknowledged within 2 business days.

Section 8: Documentation
Update the Status column to 'Routed to [handler]' after routing.

